From f0eb8a441b4efb2e197438dc958f2b2fd4fc8705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CaeliGlow <caeliglow@mockifylab.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:28:42 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] caeliglow: own config/state/cache/socket namespace by default

CaeliGlow previously read and wrote the stock Noctalia user directories
(~/.config/noctalia, ~/.local/state/noctalia, runtime sockets), so it
behaved like a re-skinned Noctalia instead of its own product. Every
persistent and runtime path now defaults to the caeliglow namespace:

- FileUtils::configDir/stateDir/dataDir resolve to ~/.config/caeliglow,
  ~/.local/state/caeliglow and ~/.local/share/caeliglow. New
  CAELIGLOW_CONFIG_HOME / CAELIGLOW_STATE_HOME / CAELIGLOW_DATA_HOME
  overrides; the legacy NOCTALIA_*_HOME vars still work as an explicit
  escape hatch, and tests that pin them keep passing.
- IPC socket, single-instance lock and dmenu socket use caeliglow-* so
  CaeliGlow can run beside a live stock Noctalia without talking to (or
  blocking) it.
- Log file moves to $XDG_CACHE_HOME/caeliglow/caeliglow.log; calendar
  cache to caeliglow/calendar.
- config replay (support reports) reconstructs the caeliglow layout.

With a fresh ~/.config/caeliglow the shell starts on CaeliGlow compiled-in
defaults (hover-to-open panels, power pill, launcher avatar). No stock
Noctalia file is ever read, migrated, or overwritten.
